</DIV></DIV>
<P>(ix) The after-flame time of the specimen shall be recorded to the nearest 0.2-second and the char length to the nearest 0.1-inch (.3 cm).</P>
<P>E. <I>Report.</I> (i) The after-flame time and char length of the sample unit shall be the average of the results obtained from the individual specimens tested. All values obtained from the individual specimens shall be recorded.</P>
<P>(ii) The after-flame time shall be reported to the nearest 0.2-second and the char length to the nearest 0.1-inch (.3 cm).</P>
<P>F. <I>Source.</I> These test requirements are contained in &#x201C;Federal Test Method Standard 191, Method 5903 (1971)&#x201D; and are reproduced for your convenience.</P>
